# Triggers music-stack-auto-sync.service whenever an iPod Video (5th/5.5th
# gen) enumerates on the USB bus — idVendor/idProduct confirmed live
# against a real device (see notes.md,
# docs/iopenpod-artworkdb-missing-mhii-chunk.md).
#
# Matches the USB device ADD event itself, not the mounted block device —
# this fires well before udisks2/the desktop environment has finished
# auto-mounting the filesystem. Waiting for the mount to actually appear
# (and auto-mounting it if nothing else does) is `sync-orchestrator
# auto-sync`'s own job (--wait-seconds, mount_candidate_devices()), not
# this rule's — see services/sync-orchestrator/README.md.
#
# TAG+="systemd" + ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}=... (not RUN+=) is deliberate: a
# RUN+= script is executed inside systemd-udevd's own per-device cgroup,
# which gets killed once udev considers that device's event handling
# finished — confirmed live, a RUN+= + `setsid ... &` script visibly
# started (it successfully auto-mounted the device) but vanished with
# zero log output before the actual sync could run or flush anything.
# TAG+="systemd" hands the device off to systemd instead, which starts
# music-stack-auto-sync.service as a fully independent unit, immune to
# udev's own process/cgroup lifecycle.
#
# If you sync a different iPod generation, add another ATTR{idProduct}=="..."
# line for its PID. Two are confirmed live so far against real devices on
# a real multi-profile deploy (see notes.md's 2026-09-29 entry): 5th/5.5th
# gen iPod Video (0x1209) and 6th/7th gen iPod Classic (0x1261). A
# profile's device.match_by/match_value (a real Apple product serial) is
# unrelated to the USB PID family its iPod enumerates under, so a
# correctly-matched profile still silently never triggers auto-sync if
# its device's generation isn't listed below.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTR{idProduct}=="1209", \
    TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="music-stack-auto-sync.service"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTR{idProduct}=="1261", \
    TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="music-stack-auto-sync.service"
